From a2c8910f5d80514e692bd239aa278b8c36f7874a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 18:42:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] www, httpd: USB Application, Media Server, Samba and FTP
 pages on the Reaper kit (102.8 line)

The four USB Application pages as Reaper kit pages over the stock handlers; the stock pages still
ship and stay reachable from the menu group until each is reviewed on hardware.
- Reaper_USBApps.asp: one card per USB service (Samba, FTP, Media Server, Printer, Time Machine,
  mobile broadband, USB disks) with its state, and the disks with their partitions, size and use.
- Reaper_Samba.asp: the server switch, name, workgroup, protocol range, simpler share names,
  master browser, WINS and user limit; guest access or accounts; the accounts, folders and
  per-folder rights.
- Reaper_FTP.asp: the server switch, WAN access (asks first), anonymous or accounts, TLS (never
  with anonymous), user limit, file-name encoding; a note when a port forward takes port 21; the
  same accounts and rights.
- Reaper_MediaServer.asp: DLNA and iTunes servers, names, rescan, status page, and the media
  folders with their types (ten at most, picked from the disks, a folder can be made there); live
  scan status.
- reaper/rp.share.js: the shared part - the disk / folder / account model from the stock emitters
  (never the page status emitter that prints raw folder names), the stock /aidisk handlers for
  accounts, folders and rights, and the account and rights editor both pages use. Deleting a
  folder asks for DELETE typed: it removes every file in it.
- menu.js: the kit pages take the four tabs; the stock pages are inherit tabs of the group. httpd
  lists the four pages as Reaper-native. 25 language packs: RUSB_1..33.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
